WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:08.720
Hi, Mystery Recapped here. Today I am going to&nbsp;
explain a South Korean film called “Deranged.”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:19.440
Spoilers ahead! Watch out and take care!
Dr. Jae-Hyuk is a former professor of biochemistry&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:25.600
from Seoul and a father of two. He lost his&nbsp;
life savings and job due to a bad investment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:30.160
he made in the stock market on the advice&nbsp;
of his detective younger brother Jae-Pil.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:36.080
Jae-Pil regrets squandering Jae-hyuk's money&nbsp;
in the stock market and has apologised to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:42.080
him many times but Jae-Hyuk refuses to accept&nbsp;
his apology and wants nothing to do with him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.080 --> 00:00:47.680
Jae-hyuk currently works as a pharmaceutical&nbsp;
sales representative for ChoA Pharmaceuticals,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:53.280
which involves doing a lot of menial tasks&nbsp;
like taking his boss James Kim’s family on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:57.920
trips and kissing his client’s feet. Seeing&nbsp;
Jae-Hyuk overworked and stressed all the time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.920 --> 00:01:02.800
his wife has offered to pick up a job to help&nbsp;
him support the family on many occasions but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:08.880
his pride doesn’t allow him to make his wife work.&nbsp;
Remorseful, Jae-Pil continues to look for ways to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:14.560
pay his brother back. He notices strange stock&nbsp;
activity of ChoA Pharmaceuticals and tries to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:19.360
warn Jae-Hyuk about it but the latter doesn’t&nbsp;
want to take any more advice from his brother.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:24.480
ChoA Pharmaceuticals has been bought by a&nbsp;
foreign-based firm called BronStar, which has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:31.200
shut down its R&amp;D department to cut costs. Jae-Pil&nbsp;
seeks his biochemist girlfriend and Jae-Hyuk’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:37.200
friend Yeon-joo’s help to pay his brother back but&nbsp;
she refuses to get screwed over like Jae-Hyuk.
&nbsp;

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:43.040
One night, Jae-Hyuk finds his wife and children&nbsp;
eating in the middle of the night but he doesn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:48.480
think much of it and goes to sleep. The next&nbsp;
morning, an unrelated couple discovers a dead&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:54.000
body of a woman floating in the Han river and&nbsp;
alerts the police. The couple are traumatised&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.000 --> 00:02:00.480
by the discovery as the dead body is in a state&nbsp;
of cachexia i.e., reduced to skin and bones.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:06.000
This puzzles the investigators as reducing&nbsp;
someone to their skin and bone takes time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:10.480
and the woman was with her family last night&nbsp;
and went to bed with her husband before she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:16.080
was found missing in the morning. The police find&nbsp;
several more dead bodies in similar condition in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:22.480
water bodies throughout Seol, sending the media&nbsp;
and public into a frenzy. Jae-Pil is ordered to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.480 --> 00:02:28.400
go to the Gangwon province, which shares borders&nbsp;
with North Korea, to investigate similar cases.
&nbsp;

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:34.800
Meanwhile, Jae-Hyuk could care less and goes to&nbsp;
his scheduled golf trip with his boss Kim. At the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:40.400
Golf Course, Kim keeps gulping down bottle after&nbsp;
bottle of water. Jae-Hyuk and his coworkers do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:46.560
not think much of it until Kim makes a run for the&nbsp;
pond and jumps into it almost as if some invisible&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:52.000
force was making him do it. Jae-Hyuk tries to&nbsp;
save him but without success and just like the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:58.320
other bodies, it doesn’t take long for Kim’s body&nbsp;
to be reduced to skin and bones. After his boss’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:03.840
tragic death, Jae-Hyuk returns home late to find&nbsp;
his family guzzling water in a similar manner. 
&nbsp;

00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:09.440
By the next day, several more bodies pile up&nbsp;
throughout the country, finally attracting the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.440 --> 00:03:13.840
Korean government’s attention. The authorities&nbsp;
have a hard time understanding the cause&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:19.200
of the sudden deaths because the victims do not&nbsp;
show any physical symptoms but look gruesome as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:24.400
soon as they jump into the water. At one home,&nbsp;
the authorities find a victim dead in his bathtub&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:30.000
with unidentifiable worm-like organisms swimming&nbsp;
next to his dead body. The officials at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:35.040
Ministry of Health examine the organisms and&nbsp;
determine that they are parasitic horsehair&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:41.760
worms that normally use insects as hosts. These&nbsp;
worms seem to have mutated into a new form that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:47.360
allows them to infect human bodies. It is learned&nbsp;
that the sudden change in appearance of victims&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:53.360
after jumping into water bodies was caused by the&nbsp;
parasites abandoning the host bodies for water.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.360 --> 00:03:58.240
These worms can control the human brain and&nbsp;
hence the infected show symptoms of increased&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.240 --> 00:04:03.440
hunger without appropriate weight gain. When&nbsp;
the worms are mature and ready to reproduce,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.440 --> 00:04:08.880
the infected people experience excessive thirst&nbsp;
and hence they jump into the river to allow the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.880 --> 00:04:14.320
worms to come out of their bodies and procreate.&nbsp;
As the scientists look for a cure, the government&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:20.080
deploys a police force throughout Korea to prevent&nbsp;
the infected from jumping into water bodies. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.080 --> 00:04:25.840
government also urges people who have been in or&nbsp;
near water and show symptoms of hunger and thirst&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.840 --> 00:04:33.840
to rush to the nearest hospital. This results&nbsp;
in countless people rushing to hospitals. 
&nbsp;

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:39.280
After learning about these developments at work,&nbsp;
Jae-Hyuk panics and rushes home as his family&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.280 --> 00:04:44.720
showed the symptoms of the disease. A team&nbsp;
of scientists and doctors study the organism&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:49.520
and ascertain that it is impossible to&nbsp;
physically extract it from the host bodies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.520 --> 00:04:54.880
as it fuses itself to the inner walls of the&nbsp;
small intestine pretending to be part of it to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.880 --> 00:05:00.160
draw nutrients from the host. Since physical&nbsp;
extraction of the organism is not feasible,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:06.320
scientists speculate that the organism could&nbsp;
be killed by anthelmintic drugs i.e. drugs used&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:11.920
to treat infections of animals with parasitic&nbsp;
worms. The scientists set up a patient group to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.920 --> 00:05:17.680
experiment the effect of anthelmintic drugs on&nbsp;
the organism. Yeon-joo raises ethical concerns&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.680 --> 00:05:22.720
but her superiors could care less as they are&nbsp;
under intense pressure to find the cure. 
&nbsp;

00:05:22.720 --> 00:05:28.160
Word gets out about the anthelmintic drugs&nbsp;
and people crowd pharmacies to get it. Matters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:32.000
become worse and it is discovered&nbsp;
that using any type of anthelmintic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:37.280
actually causes more excruciating pain and&nbsp;
eventual death. The government immediately&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.280 --> 00:05:42.880
releases a statement advising citizens against&nbsp;
using anthelmintic drugs to treat the disease. 
&nbsp;

00:05:42.880 --> 00:05:49.040
In a Gangwon village, Jae-Pil finds the village’s&nbsp;
chief crying at a local hospital blaming himself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.040 --> 00:05:54.480
for the epidemic. When Jae-Pil asks him to explain&nbsp;
himself, the chief reveals that in the spring,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.480 --> 00:05:59.600
he saw some strangers releasing their dogs in the&nbsp;
stream. He didn’t think much of it at the time as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.600 --> 00:06:04.240
he thought the strangers were trying to get rid&nbsp;
of their sick dogs. The village was days away from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.240 --> 00:06:08.960
the tourist season and the chief didn’t want to&nbsp;
jeopardise the year's income so he didn’t inform&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.960 --> 00:06:14.000
the authorities and collected the dog’s corpses&nbsp;
and buried them in the mountain himself. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:19.360
holiday season arrived and the tourists flocked&nbsp;
to the village but nothing happened. Some months&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.360 --> 00:06:24.640
passed by and the bodies started to be discovered&nbsp;
by the stream. Jae-Pil also learns about his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.640 --> 00:06:29.680
brother’s family but is not able to be by their&nbsp;
side at the hospital because of his work duty.
&nbsp;

00:06:29.680 --> 00:06:35.840
More deaths later, a patient reveals that he was&nbsp;
cured by a specific type of drug called Windazole&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.840 --> 00:06:41.440
he took at home. Clinical tests also confirm&nbsp;
the necrosis of the mutant horsehair worm.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.440 --> 00:06:46.800
The word spreads like wildfire and the country&nbsp;
goes insane in order to get a hold of the drug.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:51.920
It is revealed that only ChoA Pharmaceuticals,&nbsp;
the company Jae-Hyuk works for, manufactures&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.920 --> 00:06:57.200
the drug. However, the company stopped the&nbsp;
production of the drug last October due to poor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.200 --> 00:07:03.040
sales. Pharmacies run out of supply within hours.&nbsp;
Government officials contact the pharmaceutical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.040 --> 00:07:08.240
company and demand that they increase supply.&nbsp;
However, ever since being acquired by the foreign&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.240 --> 00:07:12.800
investment company, the machines involved in&nbsp;
creating the drug were poorly managed and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.800 --> 00:07:18.560
company fails to manufacture a single pill. 
The company’s CEO is brought for public&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.560 --> 00:07:22.480
hearing and the government requests the&nbsp;
company to reveal the drug's composition,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.480 --> 00:07:27.280
but the CEO says that the company's major&nbsp;
foreign stockholders have refused to do so,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:27.280 --> 00:07:32.240
and the government has no legal grounds to force&nbsp;
the company to disclose the drug's "recipe"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.240 --> 00:07:37.520
either. The country’s prime minister offers the&nbsp;
company a generous amount to disclose the drug’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.520 --> 00:07:42.400
composition. He gives the company a few hours&nbsp;
to accept the offer and threatens them with a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.400 --> 00:07:47.920
scrupulous audit should they not accept the offer.&nbsp;
As the company mulls on the government’s offer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:47.920 --> 00:07:52.960
people become desperate to get their hands on&nbsp;
the drug. Jae-Hyuk uses his contacts at the ChoA&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.960 --> 00:07:57.920
pharma to get ahold of the last remaining batch&nbsp;
of the drug. However, the last remaining pills&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.920 --> 00:08:03.360
are taken away from him when a crowd of people&nbsp;
outside the company spot him with the scarce drug.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:03.360 --> 00:08:08.960
Jae-Hyuk is devastated and his coworker comforts&nbsp;
him. Jae-Hyuk’s co worker reveals that ChoA&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.960 --> 00:08:15.120
pharma released 100,000 boxes of the drug in the&nbsp;
market before its production was discontinued,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.120 --> 00:08:20.640
with each box containing four doses. Jae-Hyuk&nbsp;
finds it hard to believe that the market ran&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:20.640 --> 00:08:26.160
out of 400,000 doses within hours of the&nbsp;
announcement. His coworker speculates that maybe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.160 --> 00:08:30.880
the drugs were never released on the market. 
Meanwhile, Jae-Pil again starts looking into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.880 --> 00:08:36.800
ChoA’s shady stock activity. He learns that a few&nbsp;
individuals with no address anonymously bought all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:42.240
the stocks of the company some months back when&nbsp;
the company was not even making any profit. 
&nbsp;

00:08:42.240 --> 00:08:48.160
At the public hearing, ChoA’s CEO rejects the&nbsp;
PM’s offer, putting forth a counter offer. He&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.160 --> 00:08:53.920
asks the government to buy the entire company&nbsp;
for a whopping 5 billion won. This would make the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:53.920 --> 00:08:58.880
drug’s composition a government property and as&nbsp;
its owner, the government can disclose it to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:58.880 --> 00:09:03.680
public, which would allow other pharmaceuticals to&nbsp;
make more of it for the rapidly increasing number&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.680 --> 00:09:09.360
of patients. The price is unreasonable and most&nbsp;
government officials are against the idea but the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:09.360 --> 00:09:14.320
PM is under intense pressure to deliver the cure&nbsp;
to the people as scientists have learned that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.320 --> 00:09:20.000
infected people will die within a day even without&nbsp;
jumping into water if they don’t get the cure. 
&nbsp;

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:24.640
Upon further investigation, Jae-pil finds&nbsp;
one of the individuals who bought the stock&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:24.640 --> 00:09:29.200
of the company. The man is revealed&nbsp;
to be an ex-researcher of ChoA pharma.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:29.200 --> 00:09:33.680
Jae-Pil forces the man to tell the truth&nbsp;
and he reveals that the entire health crisis&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:33.680 --> 00:09:39.200
was planned and orchestrated by disgruntled&nbsp;
former researchers at ChoA Pharmaceuticals. 
&nbsp;

00:09:39.200 --> 00:09:44.880
Some years ago, the scientists at the pharma&nbsp;
company learned about the parasite Yeongasi.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:44.880 --> 00:09:49.680
Hoping to find a cure to other brain diseases&nbsp;
such as Alzheimer's, the researchers began&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:49.680 --> 00:09:55.680
looking into the Yeongasi parasite’s protein that&nbsp;
controls the brain. After succeeding in creating a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:55.680 --> 00:10:01.520
mutant version of the horsehair parasite that used&nbsp;
mammals as hosts, the team were set to begin their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.520 --> 00:10:06.320
research on finding the cure of Alzheimer's&nbsp;
when the company was suddenly sold over,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:06.320 --> 00:10:12.480
and new owners fired the research team. Upset&nbsp;
and angry, some of the researchers joined forces&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:12.480 --> 00:10:18.240
and planned the entire crisis. They bought the&nbsp;
stock of the company and released the parasite&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.240 --> 00:10:23.280
after storing away 100,000 packets of the&nbsp;
drug. Because of this, hundreds of thousands&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:23.280 --> 00:10:28.480
of people became infected over the summer as&nbsp;
they went to rivers for vacation. One of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:28.480 --> 00:10:33.520
scientists then acted as if he had been treated&nbsp;
by the drug in order to raise stock prices. 
&nbsp;

00:10:33.520 --> 00:10:38.480
After learning about this, Jae-pil immediately&nbsp;
calls his brother and the two go to the storage,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:38.480 --> 00:10:43.120
where the researchers had hidden the rest of the&nbsp;
drugs. The two brothers manage to get hold of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:43.120 --> 00:10:49.120
drugs but someone locks them inside the building&nbsp;
and sets it on fire. The two manage to survive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:49.120 --> 00:10:53.840
but all the drugs burns down with the building and&nbsp;
the researcher who told them about the building&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:53.840 --> 00:10:58.480
is murdered by a mysterious man.
Jae-Hyuk refuses to give up and he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:58.480 --> 00:11:02.880
decides to make the drug with his knowledge&nbsp;
of chemistry. As long as he is able to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:02.880 --> 00:11:08.400
create a drug with the same active ingredient as&nbsp;
Windazole, he should be able to treat his family&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:08.400 --> 00:11:13.360
without the Windazole. Yeon-joo ropes in&nbsp;
other pharma companies in his plans. 
&nbsp;

00:11:13.360 --> 00:11:18.240
Meanwhile, Jae-Pil’s colleagues continue looking&nbsp;
into the shady pharma company and find out that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:18.240 --> 00:11:24.400
the murdered researcher was actually the head of&nbsp;
the research team and a close friend of the CEO.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:24.400 --> 00:11:29.200
The other researchers have already fled the&nbsp;
country and the murdered team leader was also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:29.200 --> 00:11:35.120
supposed to flee after getting rid of the drugs in&nbsp;
the warehouse. The entire crisis was premeditated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:35.120 --> 00:11:41.200
and planned by the pharma’s CEO and the&nbsp;
researchers from the beginning. Unbeknownst to all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:41.200 --> 00:11:46.880
this, the prime minister accepts the CEO’s offer&nbsp;
to buy the company. However, as the PM is about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:46.880 --> 00:11:53.200
to sign the paper, he is informed about the entire&nbsp;
plot and the CEO is arrested. Jae-Hyuk and other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:53.200 --> 00:11:59.120
pharmaceutical companies join forces to hastily&nbsp;
create an effective drug and treat everyone.
&nbsp;

00:11:59.120 --> 00:12:04.160
Some months pass by. Jae-hyuk and his family&nbsp;
are spending time at an amusement park,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:04.160 --> 00:12:11.040
joking about vacationing abroad and the Yeongasi&nbsp;
worm. Jae-hyuk suddenly freezes and turns around&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:11.040 --> 00:12:15.440
as the movie ends with a scene of a dead&nbsp;
body floating in New York Harbor.
&nbsp;

00:12:16.000 --> 00:12:19.440
Subscribe for more videos like&nbsp;
this, turn on the notification,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:19.440 --> 00:12:23.760
and leave a like to help the channel&nbsp;
out. Thanks for watching. 

